-- title:
--   The orthogonal projection onto the complement of u
-- statement:
--   For every direction $u$ and vector $y$ in a real inner product space, the orthogonal projection onto the hyperplane $u^\perp$ is given by
--
--   $$
--   P_{u^\perp} y = y - \langle u, y\rangle\, u.
--   $$
--
--   This is the orthogonal part $w$ of the decomposition $z = t u + w$, $w \perp u$, used throughout section 26. It is exactly the expression appearing in the extremal function $f_N(z) = H_c(\langle u,z\rangle - 1) + \tfrac12\|z - \langle u,z\rangle u\|^2$, whose second term is $\tfrac12\|P_{u^\perp} z\|^2$, and it is the second summand of the gradient (26.3).
